{"title":"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a far-off land three fish can be traded for two loaves of bread and a loaf of bread can be traded for four bags of rice. How many bags of rice is one fish worth?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/9/049c4ba2449dc9a47f20fdb9c1dfc9d939a2a7b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\frac{3}{8} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\frac{3}{4} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 2\\frac{2}{3} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 3\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"367\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> represent one fish, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> a loaf of bread, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> a bag of rice. Then:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35ab52a07858605727284bd249e8755f5399bc43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3f=2l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/f/d7f70bce0fe425670e76141157850ac3db9e74a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l=4r$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> from the second equation back into the first gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b6133d056f43645d66a2f394eb9192a594161be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3f=8r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />. So each fish is worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/f/24f4606bd5646f403a4676964fe7fea017583c28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> bags of rice, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b10b944ed144e4cbba4db720d5ecc36a5a2129d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\frac{2}{3}\\Rightarrow \\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/JXQoEzh9eM4\">https://youtu.be/JXQoEzh9eM4</a> Soo, DRMS, NM\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_.5B.F0.9F.94.A5Fast_and_Easy.F0.9F.94.A5.5D\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Nm0zn-aXyl0\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Nm0zn-aXyl0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wi